 # PVS Compactification and Temporal Coherence Pass
-
 Also called: PVS Compactification, PVS Compactification and Output Pass, PVS Data Construction, Temporal PVS Generation
 
 ## Overview
-This compute shader pass compactifies the raw visibility indices generated by the preceding raster occlusion culling stage and constructs two distinct Potentially Visible Set (PVS) datasets: $PVS_{curr}$ and $PVS_{curr-prev}$ [S1, S2]. It solves the problem of efficiently preparing visibility data for temporal coherence by identifying blocks visible in the current frame and those newly visible since the last frame, enabling the selection of optimal occluders for subsequent rendering passes [S1, S2]. It differs from sibling methods like [Raster Occlusion Culling](1562-raster-occlusion-culling.md) by focusing on data structure construction and temporal history management rather than the initial geometric visibility test.
